  /* ── Responsive data tiers ─────────────────────────────────────────────
     One card, three densities. Each tier strictly ADDS to the one below it,
     so nothing is stated twice as the viewport grows:

       compact  (<700)      name · year · category · thumbs · arrow
       medium   (700–1023)  + intro line, location, status, tags
       expanded (>=1024)    + description, client, program, "Go to project"

     Tablet used to inherit the phone treatment wholesale: at 1023px a card
     was 331px tall and carried a 58px title with no supporting text at all,
     taller than the same card on desktop while saying less. The middle tier
     is what that space is for. */

  @media (max-width: 699.98px) {
    /* Breadcrumb bottom-docks below 700, so nothing to clear or seal. */
    .projects-fixed-wrapper { --stick-top: 0px; top: 0; }

